    "title": "World Baseball Classic locations 2026: Full list of cities, stadiums hosting WBC games in U.S., Japan",
    "text": "World Baseball Classic locations 2026: Full list of cities, stadiums hosting WBC games in U.S., Japan originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.The 2026 World Baseball Classic is set to turn the globe into a diamond once again, spanning four iconic cities across the United States, Japan, and Puerto Rico. From the historic Tokyo Dome to the World Baseball Classic debut of Houston’s Daikin Park, the tournament’s sixth installment will bring the world's most elite talent to some of the game's most passionate markets.AdvertisementThe journey to the championship officially begins on March 5, 2026, with the first-round pools divided among Tokyo, San Juan, Houston, and Miami. As the field narrows, the action will consolidate in the United States, with Houston and Miami sharing the quarterfinals before South Florida takes center stage. For the second consecutive tournament, Miami’s loanDepot park will serve as the ultimate destination, hosting the semifinals and the winner-take-all championship game on March 17.Here's the complete list of World Baseball Classic games and their locations.MORE: Full World Baseball Classic rostersWhere is the World Baseball Classic in 2026?The opening round of the World Baseball Classic will occur across four cities.PoolCityStadiumDatesPool ASan Juan, Puerto RicoHiram Bithorn StadiumMarch 6–11Pool BHouston, TexasDaikin Park (Minute Maid Park)March 6–11Pool CTokyo, JapanTokyo DomeMarch 5–10Pool DMiami, FloridaloanDepot parkMarch 6–11The knockout stages of the 2026 World Baseball Classic will be held across Houston and Miami, with the tournament increasingly consolidating in Florida as it reaches the final rounds.AdvertisementThe quarterfinals are split based on pool advancement: the top two teams from Pool A (San Juan) and Pool B (Houston) will play their quarterfinal matchups in Houston, while the top two from Pool C (Tokyo) and Pool D (Miami) will face off in Miami.RoundDateVenueLocationQuarterfinal 1Friday, March 13loanDepot parkMiami, FLQuarterfinal 2Friday, March 13Daikin ParkHouston, TXQuarterfinal 3Saturday, March 14Daikin ParkHouston, TXQuarterfinal 4Saturday, March 14loanDepot parkMiami, FLOnce the field is narrowed to the final four, the entire tournament moves to Miami for the duration of the championship round.RoundDateVenueLocationTime (ET)Semifinal 1Sunday, March 15loanDepot parkMiami, FL8:00 p.m.Semifinal 2Monday, March 16loanDepot parkMiami, FL8:00 p.m.World Championship FinalTuesday, March 17loanDepot parkMiami, FL8:00 p.m.MORE: Which MLB players have had more than 3,000 career strikeouts?Where is the 2026 World Baseball Classic championship?The 2026 World Baseball Classic championship will be held in Miami, Florida, at loanDepot park, the home of the Miami Marlins.AdvertisementThe tournament culminates there on Tuesday, March 17, 2026, with the first pitch scheduled for 8:00 p.m. ET. This marks the second consecutive time that Miami has hosted the final, following Japan's thrilling victory over Team USA in 2023.MORE: MLB teams that have never won a World Series",
